Each window renders a loop at the top of its body into a root of its own.

A reactive slot at the top of a window body renders into a root container,
and that container is what the window shows. The lowering used to synthesize
one `__root` for the whole package, so on fyne the second window's rows went
into the first window's container, and its build returned a fresh VBox of its
static siblings with no rows at all -- the first window's did the same, so on
fyne neither window showed a row. Each window now gets its own root, named by
its position among the windows (`__root`, `__root1`, ...), so a single-window
program is unchanged. State is still shared: both windows read one Model, and
a push in either re-renders only the slot that reads what it changed.

gtk4 built only the first window. It now builds every window as a
GtkApplicationWindow of its own over the one Model: BuildUI presents the rest
and returns the entry (`output(entry = …)`, else the first) for its caller to
present.

The executed half is `TestMultiWindowRootSlotsRun` in both platforms, which
reads each window's rows off the built tree and pushes in each window.

deny * `__renderSlot1\(m\.__root\)` -- window two's slot renders into its own root, not window one's
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `return container\.NewVBox\(` -- a window whose slot renders into its root returns that root, not its static siblings without the rows

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}

component Row(label string) ui.node {
    var n = 0
    ui.button(text="{label} {n}", @click { n += 1 })
}

var items = ["a", "b"]
var notes = ["x"]

ui.window #one(title="One") {
    ui.text(value="one head")
    for var it = items {
        Row(label=it)
    }
    ui.text(value="one foot")
    ui.button #more(text="more", @click { items.push("c") })
}

ui.window #two(title="Two") {
    ui.text(value="two head")
    for var it = notes {
        ui.text(value=it)
    }
    ui.text(value="two foot")
    ui.button #note(text="note", @click { notes.push("y") })
}
